{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/982363-spell-casting-saves","id":982363,"title":"Spell casting & saves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-05T14:48:12-07:00","id":982363,"title":"Spell casting & saves","content":"Still getting use to this system I'm wondering what one roll to save against on spell coming at them or is it just clash of wills. Other item I'm wondering on is what mages use for rolling damage on there spells, I thought intelligent for pictured how its suppose to work. Dicepool I imagine may very on attributes an skills for whatever your trying to cast, am I correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12294-haloth","name":"Haloth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12294_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:00:51-07:00","id":982377,"title":"","content":"Part 1 Spells are usually withstood, and can be counterspelled. Se pages 127 and 192.<br /> <br /> Part 2 You don't roll any damage separatly from the spell, the damage is usually part of he spell design and equal to potency. The exception is if the damage is caused by the effects of the spell for example if you use a spell to throw a care at someone the car deals the damage not the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7463,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","user":"Toine","date":".  For better answer. 10-05-2016, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:35:50-07:00","id":982402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haloth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/982363-spell-casting-saves#post982363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still getting use to this system I'm wondering what one roll to save against on spell coming at them or is it just clash of wills. Other item I'm wondering on is what mages use for rolling damage on there spells, I thought intelligent for pictured how its suppose to work. Dicepool I imagine may very on attributes an skills for whatever your trying to cast, am I correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills is indeed the closest thing to a save that anyone would normally get against Awakened magic, though keep in mind that someone only gets to Clash if they have something, or proceed to use something that might theoretically counter the magical effect in question. For example, if a Mage tries to mind control someone, the only way to Clash with that is to use an effect (most likely a supernatural effect) that might overcome said mind control, like a mental shield or an already active mind controlling effect on the subject.<br /> <br /> Other than that, most non-direct damage spells can be Withstood, which subtracts a relevant resistance stat (Resolve, Stamina, or Composure) from the Potency of the Mages spell. Generally, as long as the Mage gets a single success the spell then takes effect at whatever Potency it currently rests at.<br /> <br /> As for how much damage it does, Toine's pretty much spot on. Direct damage spells deal their Potency in damage and are never Withstood, while other effects deal damage as determined by the situation. For example, lightning an area that someone happens to reside in does damage as per the core fire rule, and Teleporting someone a mile up and letting them fall deals damage as per the falling rules.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess I should also specify that the dice pool for all Awakened magic is Gnosis + the spells Primary Arcanum. You can add a limited number of bonuses to the base pool (usually in the form of Yantras or Willpower), but that's always going to be the base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-05-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T17:18:47-07:00","id":982448,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick replies. Next step is to figure out how a Paradox or rather happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12294-haloth","name":"Haloth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12294_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:09:35-07:00","id":982500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haloth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/982363-spell-casting-saves?p=982448#post982448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the quick replies. Next step is to figure out how a Paradox or rather happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you cast a spell with an obvious magical effects in front of one or more Sleeper witnesses, a spell you have Innured, or use more than [1 + your dots in the spell's primary Arcanum - the minimum required dots in the spell's primary Arcanum to cast it] Reach, the Storyteller gets to roll a Paradox dice pool. Each of these factors adds dice to the dice pool, as explained in the table on page 118. Additionally, multiple Sleeper witnesses add 9-again, 8-again, or the Rote quality to the dice pool, depending on how many there are. Using your Dedicated Tool as a Yantra and/or spending Mana reduces the dice pool. Even if you reduce the dice pool to 0, the Storyteller gets at least a chance die. You can choose to Contest this dice pool with a dice pool equal to your Wisdom. If you do, you take one resistant bashing damage for each success the Storyteller rolls, up to a maximum of the number of successes you roll, and if the Storyteller got more successes than you, you gain a Paradox Condition. If you don't Contest the dice pool, each success the Storyteller rolls gives the Storyteller 1 Reach that they can use to fuck with your spell, create Abyssal Tilts, or summon Abyssal entities, as explained in the table on page 116. Each time the Storyteller rolls a Paradox dice pool, they cumulatively add one additional die to each subsequent Paradox dice pool they roll in the same scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-05-2016, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}